++### Setting-by-Setting Technical Paragraphs: Remote Runners Fleet
++
++- **hostname and pool_slug:** The runner hostname uniquely identifies the physical or virtual execution host (for example, `worker-01.internal.test`). The pool slug groups runners into specialized task fleets (such as `default` or `gpu-compute`), enabling workflows to direct heavy verification suites to properly provisioned worker infrastructure.
++- **enrollment_token:** Ephemeral, single-use authentication token minted via `POST /api/v1/admin/agent-runners/enrollment-tokens`. Token lifetime is strictly capped between 60 and 900 seconds (maximum 15 minutes). The token is consumed immediately upon successful certificate signing; replaying an expired or consumed token is rejected with HTTP 401 `ENROLLMENT_TOKEN_INVALID`.
++- **client_cert_sha256_hex:** The cryptographic SHA-256 digest of the X.509 client certificate generated during runner daemon enrollment. The orchestrator registers this fingerprint in the database, verifying that incoming mutual TLS connections match the approved hardware certificate.
++- **cert_expires_at:** The expiration timestamp for the signed client certificate (standard 30-day validity). When a certificate approaches expiration, the runner must be re-enrolled using a freshly minted token.
++- **status and heartbeats:** Reflects runner operational status (`online`, `offline`, or `revoked`). Active daemons send periodic `HeartbeatFrame` packets every 15 seconds over the established mTLS WebSocket channel. If no heartbeat is received within 45 seconds (`DEAD_EVICTION_S = 45.0`), the runner transitions to `offline`, and pending tasks are rescheduled.
++- **unprivileged_daemon_and_posix_permissions:** The runner daemon (`kanban-agent-runner`) executes as an unprivileged, non-root system account. Local cryptographic assets are created with strict POSIX file permissions: state directory `0o700` (`drwx------`), private key `client.key` `0o600` (`-rw-------`), root CA bundle `ca.pem` `0o600` (`-rw-------`), and client certificate `client.crt` `0o644` (`-rw-r--r--`).
++- **mtls_pop_handshake:** Mutual TLS connections connect to dedicated port `:8444` (or WebSocket route `/api/v1/agent-runners/ws`). During handshake, the orchestrator issues a `ChallengeHelloFrame` containing an ephemeral nonce. The runner signs the canonical challenge payload `kb-runner-pop-v1:{runner_id}:{nonce}:{cert_sha256}` using its private EC key, proving certificate possession before transitioning to `online`.
++- **runner_revocation:** Administrators can instantly revoke rogue or decommissioned runners via `POST /api/v1/admin/agent-runners/:id:revoke`. Revocation immediately terminates active WebSocket connections and flags the certificate fingerprint as revoked. Subsequent connection attempts are rejected with HTTP 403 Forbidden.
+ 
+ > [!NOTE]
+-> **Runner Certificate Rotation Lifecycle:** Runner client certificates are hardware-bound and cannot be silently renewed. To rotate a certificate, revoke the runner in `/admin/agent-runners` (AAL2 challenge confirmed), mint a fresh enrollment token (15-minute TTL), and re-enroll the runner daemon.
++> **Runner Certificate Rotation Lifecycle:** Runner client certificates are hardware-bound and cannot be silently renewed in place. To rotate a certificate, revoke the runner in `/admin/agent-runners` (AAL2 challenge confirmed), mint a fresh enrollment token (15-minute TTL), and re-enroll the runner daemon.
